'''Light freighters''' were a type of [[freighter]] used during the final [[Standard day|days]] of the [[Galactic Republic]]<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> and during the rule of the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref> The ''[[Ghost]]'', a starship owned by [[Hera Syndulla]] and used by [[Spectres|rebels]] from [[Lothal]], was a modified [[VCX-100 light freighter]].<ref name="VG">''[[Star Wars Rebels: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> The ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'', a [[Smuggler|smuggling]] ship owned by [[Han Solo]] that later became part of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]], was a [[YT-1300 light freighter]].<ref name="Encyc">{{SWE|technology|millenniumfalcon|''Millennium Falcon''}}</ref>

==History==
[[File:GhostLiveAction-Fathead.png|thumb|left|250px|The ''Ghost'' was a VCX light freighter.]]
Light freighters have been in production since at least around [[56 BBY]], at which time the YT-1300 known as the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'' was manufactured by the [[Corellian Engineering Corporation]].<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> These [[Starship|ships]] were fairly common in [[the galaxy]], being used to transport all sorts of goods (legal and otherwise) to and from worlds such as [[Naboo]],<ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref> Coruscant,<ref name="Episode III" /> and Kessel.<ref name="Episode IV" /> These freighters continued to be in use, in both transport and combat roles, well into the [[Galactic Civil War]]. Later, the ''Falcon'' saw action in the [[Cold War]].<ref name="Episode VII">{{Film|VII}}</ref> During the [[Clone Wars]], [[Trandoshan]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Bossk'wassak'Cradossk|Bossk]] piloted a [[YV-666 light freighter]] christened the ''[[Hound's Tooth]]''.<ref name="SWE">{{SWE|technology|houndstooth|''Hound's Tooth''}}</ref> [[Lux Bonteri]] used [[XS stock light freighter]]s to deploy [[Onderon rebels|Onderonian rebels]] into battle.<ref name="Galactic Defense">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Defense]]'' {{C|[[:File:Galactic_Defense_shutdown.png|shutdown date]]}}</ref>

During the Republic Era, the [[EML-850 light freighter]] was designed and prototyped. However, it had an exterior plating of [[durasteel]] which made the craft durable but very expensive. This led to the design being rejected for mass production.<ref name="Star Wars Outlaws">''[[Star Wars Outlaws]]''</ref>

During the [[Imperial Era]], the [[Spectres]] operated a [[VCX-100 light freighter]] known as the ''[[Ghost]]'', which served as their mobile headquarters and home. Flown by [[Twi'lek]] [[captain]] [[Hera Syndulla]], the ship and its crew took part in dozens of missions aimed at undermining Imperial rule.<ref name="Machine in the Ghost">{{Rebels|The Machine in the Ghost}}</ref> In [[2 BBY]], [[Mart Mattin]] owned a [[YT-2400 light freighter]] named ''[[Sato's Hammer]]''. He led a small rebel cell known as [[Iron Squadron]], which conducted a low-intensity guerrilla campaign against the Imperial presence on [[Mykapo]].<ref name="Iron Squadron">{{Rebels|Iron Squadron (episode)}}</ref> Other freighter captains operated models such as the [[Allanar N3 light freighter]] in different locations around [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Thrawn: Treason">''[[Thrawn: Treason]]''</ref>

During the period leading up to the cold war, the [[human]] [[scavenger]] [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] flew a [[690 light freighter]] for a short time.<ref name="Before the Awakening">''[[Before the Awakening]]''</ref>

